course: dictionary
lesson: 3527
title: Fear and the words for it
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Fear is the feeling you have when you think something bad or dangerous might happen. Your heart beats fast and your body gets ready to run or fight. That is useful, because fear warns you of danger. Everyone feels fear sometimes.
explain: A fear is one particular thing that frightens you, like a fear of spiders or a fear of the dark. In «Alice is called a serpent by the Pigeon», the Pigeon's fear is about snakes, because snakes eat birds' eggs.
explain: To fear something means to be afraid of it. You can also fear that something bad is true, as in «I fear we are late.» Fearful means full of fear, and fearless means having no fear. Being brave does not mean having no fear; it means doing the right thing even when you feel afraid.
fact: Fear is the feeling you get when something bad or dangerous might happen.
fact: Fear can be a noun (a fear of spiders) or a verb (to fear the dark).
fact: «Fearful» means full of fear; «fearless» means without fear.
fact: Being brave means doing the right thing even when you feel fear.
fact: «Fears usually get smaller when you face them in small, safe steps with support.»
exercise: In «Grief can come out as sadness, anger, tiredness, fear or even laughing», what is fear? | A colour | A place where people go | A kind of food | *A feeling
exercise: Which word means without any fear? | Feared | Fearful | Fearing | *Fearless
exercise: «I fear we are late.» What does fear mean here? | *To worry that something bad is true | To run very fast | To be very happy | To hide under a bed
test: According to «Fears usually get smaller when you face them in small, safe steps with support», what makes fears get smaller? | Running away each time | *Facing them in small, safe steps with support | Ignoring them completely | Hiding from them in the dark
test: In «Respect means people value and trust you; fear means people avoid you or obey you only while you are there», what does fear mean? | People trust you and want to be with you | People are laughing with you | *People avoid you or obey you only while you are there | People are sleeping near you
exam: Why is the Pigeon's fear real for birds, according to the sentences? | Snakes build nests in trees for birds | Pigeons eat snakes | Birds are too big for snakes to eat | *Snakes eat birds' eggs
